		}		</style>	</head>	<body>		<p>Hello ::PERSON_NAME::,</p>		<p>You have been granted access to the ::SOLUTION:: database.</p>		<p>Please follow the instructions below to gain access to the database.</p>		<p>Firstly, you&#8217;ll need to have FileMaker Pro 12 installed. If you don&#8217;t already have this application then you will have to contact IT Support to obtain a copy.</p>		<p>Once you have FileMaker Pro installed, follow these steps to open the database:</p>		<ol>			<li>				From the <em>File</em> menu, choose <em>Open Remote.</em> You'll be presented with the following dialog.<br/>				‡‡CODE[15]‡‡			</li>			<li>				Ensure that <em>Favorite Hosts</em> is selected in the <em>View</em> field. Then click the <em>Add</em> button.			</li>			<li>				A new dialog will appear (see below). Enter the following value for <em>Host's Internet Address: </em> ::SERVER_ADDRESS::<br/>				The <em>Favorite Host's Name</em> value can be whatever you wish.<br/>				‡‡CODE[16]‡‡			</li>			<li>				Click <em>Save</em> and you should be back at the first screen.<br/>			</li>			<li>				Select your new entry from the <em>Hosts</em> list on the left.			</li>			<li>				From the <em>Available Files</em> list on the right, select <em>::SOLUTION::</em>. Then click <em>Open</em>.			</li>			<li>				Enter the following credentials:<br/>				<table>					<tr><td>Account Name:</td><td><b>::ACCOUNT::</b></td></tr>					<tr><td>Password:</td><td><b>::PASSWORD::</b></td></tr>				</table>			</li>			<li>				You will then be asked to change your password. This only happens the first time you log in. Enter a secure (but <a href="http://xkcd.com/936/">memorable</a>!) password and continue into the database.			</li>		</ol>		<p>Let me know if you have any questions or need help.</p>		<p>::ADMIN_NAME::<br/>::ADMIN_EMAIL::</p>	</body></html>/9j/4AAQSkZJRgABAQEAkACQAAD/2wBDAAQDAwQDAwQEAwQFBAQFBgoHBgYGBgwJCQcKDw0PDw4NDg4QEhcUEBEWEQ4OFBwUFhgZGhoaEBMdHxwZHhcaGhn/2wBDA